  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 3-O-Methylgallic acid and SK-VLB, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. The drug 3-O-Methylgallic acid is identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion. All of these intermediates ultimately target SK-VLB, indicating a potential pathway where 3-O-Methylgallic acid may influence SK-VLB through these molecular intermediates. The high scores across the paths suggest that the relationship is robust, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence points to a possible dependency on these intermediates, but the precise role of 3-O-Methylgallic acid in this cascade is not fully elucidated.",
